tgies/klattsch @ 63dc2c6 (MIT), vendored with patches:
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TR=ms] sets the formant transition into steady phonemes (default 35 ms, at most 40% of the phoneme; with TR, up to 90%)
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [AV=x] scales loudness (the synth's gain, default 3.5) and glides with the phoneme's transition
  src/engine/sequencer.js: a stop's bank entry may set burstMs (default 25 ms for all)
  src/engine/synth-core.js: shaped, per-parameter transitions: a schedule event may carry curve (1 raised cosine, 2 ease-out) and params
    (the parameters it moves; the others keep their own transitions); a schedule without either renders through the original code
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TC=n] gives every event that curve; [CO=x] coarticulation: formants move in their own events, a vowel starts at
    and ends toward each neighbouring consonant's locus-equation value F + x (k F + c - F) ([COR=x] at VC; [COCV=ms], [COVC=ms]; [TCF=n]
    the formant events' curve), from bank fields vowel, locus {F1..F3: [k, c]}, locusVC, locusBurst (a stop's burst at the vowel's onset
    formants), transparent (HH: the next vowel's formants), smooth (liquids: no step); under [CO] formant events never go back in
    time and the schedule is sorted by time (stably); without [CO]/[TC] the schedule is unchanged
  src/engine/dsp.js, src/engine/synth-core.js: [GS=1] an LF (Liljencrants-Fant) voice source instead of the Rosenberg pulse: lfShape(Rd) (Fant 1995), [RD=x] [RDE=oct/effort] shape and its effort coupling, [TL=dB at 3 kHz] one-pole tilt, [JIT=%] [SHIM=%] local jitter (closure-to-closure periods) and shimmer, [AM=0..1] noise scaled by the glottal flow while voiced, [FL=x] flutter (Klatt & Klatt 1990), [NT=dB] [AT=dB] one-pole low-pass of the frication / aspiration noise (Klatt's soft low-pass noise); without GS (or GS=0) every sample is as before
  src/engine/sequencer.js: a stop's bank entry may set closure ({fields, inMs, fade}: what sounds while the tract is closed instead of
    silence, e.g. a voice bar: the parameters it sets reached in inMs (default 20, at most 40% of the closure), its A1-A3 times fade by the
    release; under [CO] the formants it sets in a formant event, the others at the vowel's VC boundary) and release: false (no burst, the
    closure fills the slot: an unreleased stop); klattsing's "stops" option generates such entries. An entry without them renders as before
